MATHEMATICAL FOUNDATIONS:
- 676+ parametric surface equations with validated implementations
- Unified geometry engine supporting Euclidean and non-Euclidean spaces
- Advanced topological surface generation (Klein bottles, Möbius strips, minimal surfaces)
- Riemann surface implementations for complex mathematical visualization
- Quantum parametric functions bridging classical and quantum mathematics

ALGORITHMIC BRIDGES:
- Real-time conversion between mathematical equations and 3D geometry
- Cross-domain algorithm translation (physics ↔ biology ↔ economics)
- Automated proof verification systems with cryptographic validation
